    selftest=[
        ("What is the difference between `cd work` and `cd /work`?", "`cd work` is relative: it goes into a `work` directory inside the current one. `cd /work` is absolute: it goes to a `work` directory directly under the root."),
        ("Why does `find . -name *.log` sometimes behave strangely and how do you fix it?", "The shell expands `*.log` against the current directory before `find` runs. Quote the pattern: `find . -name \"*.log\"`."),
        ("What is the exit code of a successful command, and how do you read it?", "0. Read it with `$?` immediately after the command."),
        ("What does `cmd 2>&1 | tee out.txt` do?", "Sends stderr to stdout, then pipes the combined stream into `tee`, which shows it on screen and saves it in `out.txt`."),
        ("What permissions does mode 640 give?", "Owner read and write, group read, others nothing."),
        ("Why can you not enter a directory that you can list?", "Entering a directory needs the execute bit; listing only needs read. Without `x` you cannot reach anything inside."),
        ("Why does `rm` not ask for confirmation, and what is the safe habit?", "Unix assumes you mean what you type; there is no recycle bin. Run `ls` with the same arguments first, use `rm -i`, or move files to a temporary folder before deleting."),
        ("What is the difference between `&&` and `;`?", "`;` always runs the next command. `&&` runs it only if the previous one succeeded."),
    ],
